# Every GPG blob, wherever it lands. hardware.md was ignored by exact name only,
# so a stray encrypted copy of it in the repo root (hardware_20260930_123947.md.gpg,
# found 2026-09-30) was untracked but NOT ignored - one `git add -A` from being
# committed. backup_hardware_md.sh and the Vaultwarden backup both write .gpg, and
# nothing encrypted belongs in this repo, so ignore the suffix outright rather
# than chase each producer's naming.
*.gpg
